### Step 1: Create the User Table

First, run the following command to generate the User migration file:
```bash
php artisan make:migration create_users_table --create=users
```

Edit the generated migration file located at `database/migrations/xxxx_xx_xx_create_users_table.php`.

Add the following content inside the `up()` method:
```php
public function up()
{
    Schema::create('users', function (Blueprint $table) {
        $table->id();
        $table->string('name');
        $table->string('email')->unique();
        $table->timestamp('email_verified_at')->nullable();
        $table->string('password');
        $table->rememberToken();
        $table->timestamps();

        // Add foreign key constraints for relationships with other tables
        $table->unsignedBigInteger('cars_id')->nullable();
        $table->foreign('cars_id')->references('id')->on('cars')->onDelete('set null');

        $table->unsignedBigInteger('pets_id')->nullable();
        $table->foreign('pets_id')->references('id')->on('pets')->onDelete('set null');

        $table->unsignedBigInteger('house_id')->nullable();
        $table->foreign('house_id')->references('id')->on('houses')->onDelete('set null');
    });
}
```

